</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Hankinson</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Caffeine, alcohol, smoking, and the risk of incident epithelial ovarian cancer</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>2008</year><volume>112</volume><fpage>1169</fpage><lpage>1177</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer||112|1169||bib31|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18213613</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tworoger</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>IM</given-names></name><name><surname>Buring</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Pollak</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name><name><surname>Hankinson</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Insulin-like growth factors and ovarian cancer risk: a nested case-control study in three cohorts</article-title><source>Cancer Epidemiol Biomarkers Prev</source><year>2007b</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>1691</fpage><lpage>1695</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Epidemiol Biomarkers Prev||16|1691||bib32|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17684148</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="fig1"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Figure drawing used to assess body fatness at ages 5 and 10 years.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="tiff" xlink:href="6604742f1"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Timing of body size assessments and numbers of participants, cases, and person-years included in each analysis, by study population</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgro